  "properties": {
    "title": "Mapping Japan cultural heritages with OpenSource based architecture",
    "description": "Japan fascinates the world with its rich culture, materialized with a full of cultural sites in its territory as example. To protect it, the Law for the protection of cultural properties established a \u201ccultural heritage\u201d designation system, where designated places should be preserved. \r\nWith the collaboration of the Nara National Research Institute for Cultural Properties, Japan cultural heritages has been mapped as a WebGIS tool where more than 100,000 places can be visualized. \r\nIn this talk will be presented tool functionalities and technically its OpenSource based architecture.",
